  "body": "Right now these are defined as pres hints on all links: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#the-page:attr-body-link\n\nHowever it seems WebKit / Blink implement this using a prefixed system color (`-webkit-link`): https://searchfox.org/wubkat/rev/3cfd3cc13001fac410f307c48df7f01e6121fe52/Source/WebCore/css/html.css#1484\n\nIn theory, those selectors should use `LinkText` / `ActiveText` / `VisitedText` system colors: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#valdef-color-linktext etc.\n\nThis is simpler to implement in general (see https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342177).\n\nGiven the legacy nature of these attributes, I propose to make them just affect the value of `LinkText` / `ActiveText` / `VisitedText` system colors, which are the standard keywords for those colors.",
